    "narrative": "The Austin Waves offense is positioned for a high-ceiling performance tonight, anchored by the elite 83.29 efficiency score of **Gunnar Henderson**. Facing Johnson, whose 5.15 xERA represents the softest matchup on the slate, **Gunnar Henderson** benefits from a massive 19% boost in SP skill projection and an aggressive 14% platoon advantage. Joining him at the top of our output expectations are **Jackson Merrill** (75.10) and **Andy Pages** (74.01). Both outfielders draw favorable matchups against Ritchie and Rojas respectively; **Jackson Merrill**\u2019s 13% platoon boost and **Andy Pages**\u2019 high-order stability as a #2 hitter provide the necessary foundation to hunt for R and RBI production, the latter of which remains a focal point as we navigate the scarcities of our 5x5 build.\n\nWhile the lineup is largely optimized, the decision to start **Dominic Smith** (46.77) over **Josh Jung** (54.92) was the most difficult pivot of the day. Despite **Josh Jung** technically possessing a higher raw efficiency score, we are leaning into the specific platoon context and the high-leverage environment of the top half of the order. **Nolan Schanuel** (59.93) holds down the UTIL spot, narrowly edging out the bench options because his consistent contact profile against Baz provides a safer floor for our AVG category, which we cannot afford to sacrifice while chasing volume. **Jacob Wilson** remains a critical start at 63.59, as his ability to capitalize on the 11% SP skill edge against Ray makes him an essential piece of our daily efficiency goals. \n\nWe are monitoring the weather closely across the league, but no immediate postponements threaten our core starters. We continue to hold **Nasim Nunez** and **Cole Carrigg** in reserve; while their elite sprint speed is a priority for our SB deficit, the current pitching matchups against high-level arms like Luzardo forced them to the bench to preserve our game caps. If **Drake Baldwin** (58.64) struggles early against Peralta, W, we may look to shuffle the depth chart for the late-night slate, but for now, we are comfortable with the current configuration as we look to close the gap in the standings.",
